<ProseLayout title="Cookie policy" description="The cookies and browser storage the Edifice Travels website uses, what each one does, how long it lasts, and how to change your choice at any time." eyebrow="Legal" updated="10 October 2026">
  <p>This site uses as little as it can. Nothing here tracks you across other websites and nothing is used for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Strictly necessary (no consent needed)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lasts</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>consent</td><td>Browser storage</td><td>Remembers whether you accepted or declined analytics</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>currency</td><td>Browser storage</td><td>Remembers the currency you chose for approximate prices</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>theme</td><td>Browser storage</td><td>Remembers light or dark mode if you chose one</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
  <p>If you accept, we load Google Analytics 4 with IP anonymisation. It sets cookies beginning <code>_ga</code> that last up to 13 months and tell us, in aggregate, which pages are read and where enquiries come from. We do not use Google Signals, remarketing or advertising features.</p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>WhatsApp links open the WhatsApp app or website, which has its own policy. We do not embed social media feeds, chat widgets or video players that set cookies.</p>

  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>Clear this site's data in your browser settings and the consent question appears again on your next visit. You can also block cookies entirely; the site works without them, except that your currency and theme choices will not be remembered.</p>
</ProseLayout>
